After work, I go into a supermarket.
I quickly shop for dinner.
First, I walk to the vegetables.
I need fresh tomatoes and an onion.
Then I look for the pasta.
I take a packet of pasta from the shelf.
After that, I go to the till.
I put my things on the belt.
The cashier scans the vegetables and the pasta.
She says, "That is four euros, please."
I pay with my card.
The cashier asks, "Do you need the receipt?"
I answer, "No, thank you."
I pack the food into my backpack.
Then I go outside.
In the evening, it is very cold.
I close my jacket.
I walk quickly to my flat.
